        "title": "06 - Philosophy of Science",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nWHY IT MATTERS:\n  Practical: funding, policy, expert testimony, teaching in schools\n  Epistemic: trusting scientific authority requires knowing what counts as science\n  Legal: Daubert standard (US courts): is expert scientific testimony based on valid science?\n    Frye standard (older): accepted by relevant scientific community\n    Daubert factors: tested/testable? Peer reviewed? Error rate? Accepted by community?"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md#009",
      "path": [
        "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science, git-history:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science]",
        "canonical_path": "philosophy/06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md",
