        "root_concepts": "[philosophy, of]",
        "section": "philosophy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Philosophy of Science",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "LOGICAL POSITIVISM / VERIFICATIONISM (Vienna Circle, 1920s-30s):\n  Meaningful claims are either:\n    (1) Analytic: true by definition/logic (mathematics, logic)\n    (2) Empirically verifiable: can be tested against observation\n  Non-verifiable claims: metaphysics, theology, aesthetics (allegedly meaningless, not just false)\n  Science: verifiable claims about the world\n  Hume's fork: relations of ideas / matters of fact — precursor to same distinction"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md#010",
      "path": [
        "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science, git-history:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science]",
        "canonical_path": "philosophy/06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md",
