      },
      "text": "KEY INSIGHT — asymmetry of verification/falsification:\n    Cannot verify \"All ravens are black\" (finite observations; always more ravens to check)\n    CAN falsify \"All ravens are black\" (find one non-black raven)\n    Science proceeds by bold conjectures + attempts to refute them\n    When refuted: discard and try again; never proven, only corroborated"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md#014",
      "path": [
        "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md"
      ],
