        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Philosophy of Science",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nIMRE LAKATOS: scientific methodology of research programs; reconciles Popper with Kuhn"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md#030",
      "path": [
        "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science, git-history:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science]",
        "canonical_path": "philosophy/06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md",
        "concepts": "[philosophy, of, science]",
        "current_path": "philosophy/06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md",
        "id": "maxim:philosophy:philosophy-of-science",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "philosophy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[philosophy, of]",
        "section": "philosophy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Philosophy of Science",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "RESEARCH PROGRAM: series of theories evolving over time, sharing:\n  Hard core: central assumptions protected from refutation by convention\n    Newtonian mechanics: F=ma is not directly falsified by any anomaly\n  Protective belt: auxiliary hypotheses that absorb anomalies; can be modified\n  Negative heuristic: don't attack the hard core\n  Positive heuristic: directions for extending and developing the theory"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md#031",
      "path": [
        "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science, git-history:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science]",
        "canonical_path": "philosophy/06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md",
        "concepts": "[philosophy, of, science]",
        "current_path": "philosophy/06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md",
        "id": "maxim:philosophy:philosophy-of-science",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "philosophy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[philosophy, of]",
        "section": "philosophy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Philosophy of Science",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PROGRESSIVE vs DEGENERATIVE:\n  Progressive: program makes novel predictions that are later confirmed\n    Einstein's relativity → predicted gravitational lensing (confirmed 1919)\n    Newtonian mechanics + perturbation theory → predicted Neptune's position (confirmed)\n  Degenerative: program only explains anomalies post-hoc; no novel predictions\n    Modifying theory AFTER the fact to explain known data → not progress"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md#032",
      "path": [
        "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science, git-history:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science]",
        "canonical_path": "philosophy/06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md",
        "concepts": "[philosophy, of, science]",
        "current_path": "philosophy/06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md",
        "id": "maxim:philosophy:philosophy-of-science",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "philosophy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[philosophy, of]",
        "section": "philosophy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Philosophy of Science",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "COMPARISON WITH KUHN:\n  Lakatos: scientists are rational in protecting core; rationality survives paradigm change\n  Kuhn: incommensurability; social factors in paradigm choice\n  Lakatos: progress = scientific methodology over time tracks problem-solving; not individual decisions\n  Both: reject simple falsificationism; understand science as complex social enterprise"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md#033",
      "path": [
        "06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science, git-history:philosophy:06-philosophy-of-science]",
        "canonical_path": "philosophy/06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md",
