        "current_path": "philosophy/06-PHILOSOPHY-OF-SCIENCE.md",
        "id": "maxim:philosophy:philosophy-of-science",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "philosophy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[philosophy, of]",
        "section": "philosophy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Philosophy of Science",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "COMPARISON WITH POPPER:\n  Popper: falsification is immediate; one negative result should refute\n  Lakatos: scientists are right to hold onto research programs; immediate abandonment is not rational\n  \"Sophisticated falsificationism\": whole programs are tested over time; not individual theories\n```"
    },
